Police cars surround the scene, their flashing lights illuminating the shattered jewelry store window.  Andrea, having handed the apprehended criminals over to the GCPD, approaches the abandoned van.  She cautiously opens the back doors.  Inside, amidst scattered tools and discarded masks, she finds several crates filled with empty jewelry boxes.

ANDREA
(Examining the crates)
They were prepared to make a big haul.

She notices a crumpled piece of paper wedged between two crates.  She retrieves it, carefully unfolding the document. It's a shipping manifest, listing the contents of the crates and a delivery address: "Gotham Docks, Warehouse 17."

ANDREA
(A grim smile playing on her lips)
Bingo.

