EXT. GOTHAM CITY STREETS - NIGHT

The relentless rain continues to fall, washing away the grime of the city. Andrea walks purposefully, scanning alleyways and doorways.  She focuses her attention on areas near the known crime scenes, hoping to find something overlooked.  Near a darkened alley, she spots a discarded burner phone lying in a puddle.  She picks it up cautiously, examining it.  The screen is cracked, but the phone still powers on.  She finds a series of text messages discussing the warehouse and mentioning a "shipment" arriving soon.  A valuable piece of evidence.

Suddenly, two figures emerge from the alley, blocking her path.

THUG 1
Well, well, what do we have here?  A nosy little snoop.

THUG 2
Let's teach her a lesson.

Andrea sighs, tucking the phone safely into her coat pocket.

ANDREA
I really don't have time for this.

She swiftly dispatches the two thugs, using a combination of precise strikes and quick maneuvers.  They slump to the ground, groaning.  Andrea contacts the GCPD, reporting the incident and requesting backup.

===GAME END===
