Finn approaches the tree, sizing up the lowest branch.  He takes a running leap and grabs hold, pulling himself up with a grunt.  He climbs slowly at first, testing each branch before putting his weight on it.  Peter Pan watches from below, offering encouragement.

PETER PAN
That's it!  Use your legs, Finn!  Find your footing!

Finn gains confidence with each upward movement. He finds a good rhythm, his hands and feet working together.  He reaches a higher branch, offering a view of the surrounding forest.  He grins, feeling a sense of accomplishment.

PETER PAN
See?  Not so hard, is it?  A Lost Boy is always at home in the trees!

